{"OAuth state parameter is derived from pipeline.signature which is predictable (md5 of pipeline view class names) and doesn't provide CSRF protection - should generate cryptographically-random state, store it in pipeline state, and validate against stored value": 0.7274491786956787, "integration.metadata[\"sender\"][\"login\"] will raise KeyError if older/partial integrations exist without sender metadata or if webhook payload shape changes - should safely handle missing metadata to avoid 500 during setup": 0.9297026991844177, "Authorize URL is built via string interpolation rather than proper URL encoding - should use urlencode to ensure correct escaping": 0.7238260507583618, "Brand spelling error: uses \"Github\" instead of \"GitHub\" in error text": 0.22154241800308228, "Test assertion hard-codes full query string including parameter order and specific state value - should parse query string and assert individual parameters, then reuse parsed state for callback request": 0.6452170610427856, "Test indexes responses.calls[2] which depends on call ordering and breaks when adding new requests - should locate relevant call by URL instead": 0.6825768351554871, "Brand spelling in asserted payload uses \"Github\" instead of \"GitHub\" - should match corrected server-side message": 0.22476346790790558, "Test hard-codes specific OAuth state value into self.setup_path_2 making it fragile to pipeline changes and incompatible with randomized state - should derive state from redirect returned by init request": 0.8345975279808044, "Second install attempt test still uses self.setup_path_2 with hard-coded OAuth state - should derive state from init redirect for consistency": 0.6351631283760071, "Test constructs setup_path_2 with hard-coded OAuth state - should parse state from init redirect to avoid coupling to specific signature/value": 0.7799793481826782, "Pending-deletion test hard-codes OAuth state making it brittle and incompatible with randomized state - should derive state from init redirect": 0.7834104299545288, "Second attempt in test hard-codes OAuth state - should parse from init redirect to keep test stable": 0.4457927346229553, "Test doesn't exercise \"installation not found\" path correctly: first GET hits OAuth redirect (no GitHub installation lookup yet), second GET uses mismatched state failing in OAuth step instead - makes /app/installations/{installation_id} 404 stub ineffective and asserts wrong behavior": 0.9683788418769836, "get_user_info calls resp.raise_for_status() which will raise on non-2xx response (invalid/expired code, GitHub outage) - exception would bubble up and 500 the setup endpoint instead of returning intended error page": 0.9676356911659241, "safe_urlopen(...) can raise on network/timeout/SSL errors but isn't inside try/except - would cause 500 during installation instead of showing intended failure page": 0.9434798955917358}